### Product Similarity Service — example requests
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (by Huachao Mao).
### With it installed, a clickable "Send Request" link appears above
### each block below — click it to run that request and see the response
### in a new VS Code tab, no terminal needed.
###
### Make sure the service is running first (either `uvicorn` or Docker —
### see the main walkthrough) and listening on http://localhost:8000.

### Health check — is the process alive at all?
GET http://localhost:8000/healthz

### Readiness check — has it finished loading the dataset?
GET http://localhost:8000/readyz

### The main deliverable: find 5 products similar to a real product_id
GET http://localhost:8000/find_similar_products?product_id=26d41bdc1495de290bc8e6062d927729&num_similar=5

### Same thing, asking for 10 instead of 5
GET http://localhost:8000/find_similar_products?product_id=26d41bdc1495de290bc8e6062d927729&num_similar=10

### Error case: a product_id that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8000/find_similar_products?product_id=this-id-does-not-exist&num_similar=5

### Error case: invalid num_similar (must be between 1 and 100) -> expect 422
GET http://localhost:8000/find_similar_products?product_id=26d41bdc1495de290bc8e6062d927729&num_similar=0

### NOTE on POST: this API only defines GET endpoints, per the assignment
### spec ("GET /find_similar_products"). There is no POST route in this
### service — a POST here would 405 (Method Not Allowed). If you want a
### POST version added (e.g. accepting a JSON body like
### {"product_id": "...", "num_similar": 5} instead of query params),
### ask and it can be added as an additional endpoint.
